1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,675
What happens to a moment when chat goes crazy?

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:04,756
It ranks higher.

3
00:00:04,756 --> 00:00:06,958
It's called chat velocity clipping.

4
00:00:06,958 --> 00:00:13,499
ClipMe measures how fast chat is moving, and uses that as one signal to rank moments on Kick and Twitch.

5
00:00:14,449 --> 00:00:19,171
Loudness alone misses moments where chat explodes but the stream goes quiet.

6
00:00:19,171 --> 00:00:20,849
Chat velocity catches them.

7
00:00:21,799 --> 00:00:26,812
A chat spike moves a moment up the ranking, alongside the other signals in the model.

8
00:00:27,763 --> 00:00:33,075
Every clip comes out captioned in 9:16, and Pro adds 4:5 and 1:1.

9
00:00:34,025 --> 00:00:37,482
See how chat velocity clipping works at clipme.com.

10
00:00:37,482 --> 00:00:39,380
Paste a VOD and try it free.

